# Starlight Drive, by Ling 3.1 Flash and SZ. An original italo-disco synthwave dance track for the
# Synthwave style: a wordless vox-lead hook (the bank vox-lead) over four-on-the-floor gated drums,
# an octave-bouncing synth bass on eighth notes, bright poly-stab chords on the off-beats, a pluck
# arpeggio, and the bank choirs — ooh under the verses, aah lifting the choruses and the breakdown.
# The saw lead answers the hook between phrases instead of doubling it. 118 BPM in Bb major; the
# last chorus goes up a whole step to C major. Midnight Arcade stays moody and Underpass heroic;
# this one is major-key, sunny, and made to dance.
#
# The chord map, one symbol a bar: two-bar cells in the intro and verses, a rising Cm-Dm-Eb-F
# pre-chorus, the chorus on Bb-F-Gm-Eb, a build that ends on G (the dominant of the new key), and
# the last chorus in C major. Every pitched part follows it bar by bar.
# chords: Bb Bb F F Gm Gm F F
# chords @9: Bb Bb Gm Gm Eb Eb F F
# chords @17: Cm Dm Eb F Cm Dm Eb F
# chords @25: Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Eb F
# chords @41: Bb Bb Gm Gm Eb Eb F F
# chords @49: Cm Dm Eb F Cm Dm Eb F
# chords @57: Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Eb F
# chords @73: Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Gm Eb Bb F Eb F
# chords @89: Cm Dm Eb F Cm Dm G G
# chords @97: C G Am F C G Am F C G Am F C G F G
# chords @113: C C G G F F C C
#
# Form 1-8: intro - drums and bass, then the arp
# Form 9-16: verse - choir-ooh and stabs under the groove
# Form 17-24: pre - the pad swells in, the arp turns to sixteenths, a snare roll
# Form 25-40: chorus - the vox hook with choir-aah, the saw answering between phrases
# Form 41-48: verse2 - ooh and stabs again, the arp back
# Form 49-56: pre2 - the same build, louder
# Form 57-72: chorus2 - the hook again, wider
# Form 73-88: breakdown - the kick and bass drop; choirs and pad carry the hook
# Form 89-96: build - the kick returns, the roll climbs, the harmony rises to G
# Form 97-112: final - the whole hook up a whole step in C major
# Form 113-120: outro - the groove winds down to one last hit
#
# Human feel: the vox hook sits a few ticks behind the beat with some early pushes inside the
# phrases, the stabs land +10 to +24 late, the off-beat hats push 6 ticks early, the bass nudges
# its off-beats 2-6 ticks early, and the hats, arp, and claps carry uneven velocities.
title: Starlight Drive
composer: Ling 3.1 Flash & SZ
year: 2026
source: original
category: originals
style: synthwave
key: Bb major
tempo: 118
time: 4/4
about: A sunny italo-disco cruise: a wordless vocal hook over four-on-the-floor gated drums, an octave-bouncing bass, bright offbeat stabs, a pluck arp, and choirs that swell in, with a kick-less breakdown and a last chorus up a whole step.

